# Kubernetes Deployment (Day 23)

Kubernetes manifests for IntellMeet. They run MongoDB, the backend API and the
frontend in a dedicated `intellmeet` namespace.

## Files

| File | What it creates |
|---|---|
| `namespace.yaml` | The `intellmeet` namespace |
| `secret.yaml` | Secrets for the backend (placeholders only, never commit real values) |
| `mongo.yaml` | MongoDB StatefulSet with a 1Gi volume, plus a ClusterIP service |
| `backend.yaml` | Backend Deployment (2 replicas, health probes, resource limits), plus service |
| `frontend.yaml` | Frontend Deployment (nginx, 2 replicas), plus a LoadBalancer service |
| `hpa.yaml` | Horizontal Pod Autoscaler for the backend (2 to 6 pods at 70% CPU) |

## Architecture

```
Browser -> frontend Service (LoadBalancer :8080)
              -> frontend Pods (nginx, static React build)
Browser -> backend Service (:5000) -> backend Pods (Node/Express + Socket.io)
                                         -> mongo Service (:27017) -> MongoDB StatefulSet
```

## Prerequisites

- Docker images pushed to a registry (replace `YOUR_DOCKERHUB_USER` in
  `backend.yaml` and `frontend.yaml`)
- A cluster: Docker Desktop (Settings > Kubernetes > Enable), minikube, or a cloud cluster
- `kubectl` installed

## Build and push images

```bash
docker build -t YOUR_DOCKERHUB_USER/intellmeet-backend:latest ./Backend
docker build -t YOUR_DOCKERHUB_USER/intellmeet-frontend:latest \
  --build-arg VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api ./Frontend
docker push YOUR_DOCKERHUB_USER/intellmeet-backend:latest
docker push YOUR_DOCKERHUB_USER/intellmeet-frontend:latest
```

## Deploy

```bash
kubectl apply -f k8s/namespace.yaml
kubectl apply -f k8s/
kubectl get pods -n intellmeet
kubectl get svc -n intellmeet
```

## Verify

```bash
kubectl get pods -n intellmeet            # all pods Running
kubectl logs deploy/backend -n intellmeet # "MongoDB Connected successfully"
kubectl port-forward svc/backend 5000:5000 -n intellmeet
curl http://localhost:5000/api/health     # expect HTTP 200
```

Open http://localhost:8080 for the frontend.

## Clean up

```bash
kubectl delete namespace intellmeet
```

## Configuration

Environment values are set in `backend.yaml` (`PORT`, `MONGO_URI`, `CLIENT_URL`).
Secrets belong in `secret.yaml`. Edit the placeholder values locally and do not
commit real keys. For production, create secrets with
`kubectl create secret` or an external secret manager.

## Known limitations

- The frontend image has `VITE_API_URL` baked in at build time, so it must be
  rebuilt with the real backend URL for each environment.
- Socket.io with more than one backend replica needs sticky sessions or a Redis
  adapter so real-time events reach every client. Redis is planned but not yet added.
- MongoDB runs as a single replica without authentication. Use a managed
  database (for example MongoDB Atlas) for production.
- Manifests were written to the Day 23 plan. Test them on a cluster before
  relying on them.